so first I kind of wanted to paint a  picture of when this whole idea came up  for you did you already have the idea  before things with the dark universe  kind of went in a sour direction not at  all I mean I was very aware of this  character obviously he's a part of pop  culture but I had no desire to make an  invisible man film so then you come up  with the idea immediately after that  possibility went away didn't ya I just  finished upgrade okay and I was really  happy with the way upgrade turned out  and I kind of got bit by the action  movie bug I wanted to crash some cars  blow some things up and I went in for a  meeting with you know some of the Blum  House and universal execs and this  character was floated it was like what  do you think about the Invisible Man  I was pretty mystified as to why we were  talking about that character in  particular but immediately I started  thinking about these opportunities to  modernize the character and make him  scary for a modern audience was there  any hesitation after having so much  success with upgrade your own original  idea jumping back into something that  was I guess an adaptation or a new spin  on an iconic character yeah maybe for a  second but I realized that I could put  my own spin on it I could take this  iconic beloved character and wrap  something around it that felt like my  film you kind of have to Jedi mind trick  yourself into thinking that this is the  first time an Invisible Man stories ever  been told you know I don't want to think  about all the other versions of this  character that have gone before whether  it's TV shows movies I just want to  forget all that and think you know how  would this movie play if this was the  first time this story was being told so  know what advice would you give someone  else out there because we're bound to  see not necessarily another Invisible  Man movie but more maybe with the  Universal Monsters coming back to screen  what would advice what advice would you  give for a writer and director jumping  into that well well look personally in  my own humble opinion I think these  characters have to get back to their  roots they were scary when they first  came out and I think that a lot of these  iconic monsters Dracula the Wolfman  they've become so ubiquitous in pop  culture that it's drained all the power  out of them what I would want to do and  or what I would want to see with  characters like that is for them to  become scary again like Dracula is  supposed to be terrifying you know now I  watch cartoons where he's voiced by Adam  Sandler right it's it's more of a it's  more of a cartoonish thing now the cape  and the voice I think I think there is a  way to make these characters scary again  that's why they've lasted so long in the  popular imagination because they have  these attributes about them that stick  in our minds you know and it's about  stripping it back to that you've got to  strip it back to its core idea if you  want to make it scary success here it  was scary got under my skin and I took  it with me so thank you for that a  couple other questions for you  spiral do you have anything to do with  that no I have not had anything to do  with the soar films for quite a while  obviously I'm still friends with a lot  of the people involved yeah but I've  really taken a back seat it's a strange  thing to sort of create a movie and then  watch it go off into the wilderness  without you and well also with Chris  Rock and Sam Jackson what was your first  reaction when you heard that's the  direction the franchise was going I'll  tell you I was on a location scout for  this movie and I got a phone call from  one of the guys at Lionsgate who's a  friend of mine and when he told me about  Chris Rock I thought back to a couple of  years ago I was at a film festival party  at the Palm Springs Film Festival and my  agent much to my horror pushed me  towards Chris Rock and was like say hi  to Chris I think I said something lame  like I'm a big fan and he hears that  hundred times a day so he was like okay  and as he was walking away his agent  said to him that guy rode saw and he  like stopped in his tracks came back and  was like you wrote saw and suddenly he  was super interested and he said to me I  would love to make a soar film and I  thought it was just something that you  say in a party you know like hey I'd  love to dye my hair pink  too you just say it because the person's  got pink hair you don't wanna make them  feel bad turns out he was serious that  was not that was not an offhand thing  that he said he really did want to make  a soar film so that was the first thing  I thought about when I heard the news  was Wow Chris Rock wasn't joking I'm so  excited about that if I could squeeze in  one more we have a  lot of Aquaman fans a Collider and I  have been forced to ask this question  it's a burning question the team has  what do you think your character does  after two people jump out of his plane  like that what's the rest of his day  like I think I think he lands the plane  and assumes a different identity  different job he's just like you know  what I've got a whole backstory for this  cargo pilot that I don't want to reveal  here but I feel like a whole movie this  could spin off into its own universe I  think the cargo pilot is unexplored  territory listening James
 

